From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Correct modern-C probe and installed pkg-config include root

The existing IPv6 socket probe needs the exit declaration and an explicit int
main signature; keep its actual runtime decision rather than forcing a cache
value. Headers install to includedir/artnet and include artnet/common.h, so
consumers need includedir, not the nonexistent includedir/libartnet.

Origin: original downstream changes against atlesn/libartnet 416a83e92d150e8e0295a9aabd7ad1fb1c1689bc
Upstream-Status: Not-Submitted
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later

--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -46,10 +46,11 @@
 #       include <sys/types.h>
 #       include <sys/socket.h>
 #       include <netinet/in.h>
+#       include <stdlib.h>
         /* Make sure the definitions for AF_INET6 and struct sockaddr_in6
          * are defined, and that we can actually create an IPv6 TCP socket.
          */
-        main()
+        int main(void)
         {
                 int fd;
                 struct sockaddr_in6 foo;
--- a/libartnet.pc.in
+++ b/libartnet.pc.in
@@ -8,4 +8,4 @@
 Description: libartnet
 Requires:
 Libs: -L${libdir} -lartnet @LIBS@
-Cflags: -I${includedir}/libartnet
+Cflags: -I${includedir}
